1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 Nf6 5. Nc3 d6 6. Be2 g6 7. O-O Bg7 8.
Be3 O-O 9. Nb3 Be6 10. f4 Qc8 11. h3 Rd8 12. g4 d5 13. e5 Ne4 14. Nxe4 dxe4 15.
Qe1 f6 (15... Bxb3 16. axb3 Nd4 {was played by RH Newman on board 9 in the
same match.}) 16. exf6 (16. Nc5 Nd4 $1) 16... exf6 17. c3 f5 18. Qh4 b6 19.
gxf5 Bxf5 20. Kh2 Qc7 21. Rg1 Kh8 22. Rg2 Qe7 23. Qf2 Bf6 24. Bb5 {(The sealed
move at the end of the first day's play)} Rac8 25. Bxc6 Rxc6 26. Bd4 Bxd4 27.
Nxd4 Rc5 28. Rg3 Bc8 29. Qe3 Rf8 30. Re1 Bb7 31. Reg1 Qd6 $2 (31... Bc8 $142 {
Crown}) 32. Rf1 $2 (32. f5 $142 {Crown}) 32... b5 $4 (32... Rh5 33. Z0 Rh4 {
Crown (CHESS, Jan 1948)}) 33. a3 (33. Ne6 $1 $18) 33... a6 $2 34. Ne6 Rd5 35.
Nxf8 Qxf8 36. Qb6 $2 Qe7 37. Re3 $2 (37. f5 $1 $18 {C.Purdy}) 37... Rd6 $1 38.
Qa7 (38. Qa5 $5) 38... Rd2+ 39. Kh1 Qc7 40. Kg1 g5 {["Now Black seems to win
in every variation" (Crown)]} 41. Rg3 $2 (41. Rf2 $1 $11 {Fritz8} Rxf2 42. Kxf2
Qxf4+ (42... gxf4 $4 43. Rxe4 $18) 43. Ke1 $11) 41... gxf4 $19 42. Rg4 (42. Qe3
{(! - Lajos Steiner, 'Chess World', Jan 1948, p7)} Rd1 $1 {Crown/Fritz8} 43.
Kg2 $1 Qb8 $1 (43... Rxf1 $4 44. Qd4+ {mates}) (43... Rd3 44. Qxf4 e3+ 45. Kg1
Qxf4 46. Rxf4 Rd1+ 47. Rf1 e2 {also wins}) 44. Rxf4 (44. Qxf4 e3+ $1 (44...
Qxf4 $2 45. Rxf4 e3+ 46. Rgf3 e2 47. Rf8+ Kg7 48. R8f7+ {draws}) 45. Kh2 Qxf4
46. Rxf4 Rh1#) (44. Qc5 e3+ 45. Rff3 fxg3 $19)) 42... f3 43. Rf2 Rd3 44. Rf1 e3
45. Rxf3 Rd1+ 46. Rf1 Rxf1+ 0-1

